      "explanation": "Here \\(\\log\\) denotes the common logarithm, with base \\(10\\). To express the answer using \\(\\log2\\), write \\(125=(10/2)^3\\). The power and quotient rules give\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log125\n&=3\\log\\left(\\frac{10}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=3(\\log10-\\log2)\\\\\n&=\\boxed{3-3\\log2},\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nsince \\(\\log10=1\\). The answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
